'''Myto's Arrow''' was a backwater [[hyperspace route]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories]] and [[New Territories]] regions of [[the galaxy]]. It looped from the [[planet]] [[Dantooine]] in [[Dantooine system]] of the [[Raioballo sector]] to the astronomical object [[Jaemus system|Jaemus]]<ref name="BM37" /> on the [[Braxant Run]].<ref name="GM" /> Despite Dantooine also being a part of the longer [[Veragi Trade Route]], the world was considered hard to reach, with Myto's Arrow as the quicker of the two routes leading there. The route shared is name with the Outer Rim [[Myto sector]]<ref name="BM37" /> and was located in grid squares L-4 and K-4 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="GM">[[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]], based on corresponding data for [[Dantooine]] and [[Jaemus system|Jaemus]].</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Myto's Arrow was first mentioned in "[[Guide to the Galaxy]]: Visiting Dantooine," an article in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 37|thirty-seventh]] issue of the ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'' magazine,<ref name="BM37" /> which was published around [[September 16]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate18">{{BuildFalconDates|37}}</ref>

The [[Myto's Arrow/Legends|route]] originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where it was first mentioned in the short story "[[Blaze of Glory (short story)|Blaze of Glory]]," which was written by [[Tony Russo]] and published by [[West End Games]] in the [[Star Wars Adventure Journal 8|eighth issue]] of ''[[Star Wars Adventure Journal]]'' in [[November]] [[1995]].<ref name="AJ8">{{JournalCite|8|Blaze of Glory (short story)}}</ref> It was then pictured for the first time in the [[2009]] reference book ''[[The Essential Atlas]]'', which was written by [[Jason Fry]] and [[Daniel Wallace]].<ref name="TEA">''[[The Essential Atlas]]''</ref>

